Q: How can I make Flexbox children 100% height of their parent? A: <h2>Use <code>align-items: stretch</code></h2>
<p>Similar to <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/15381172/how-can-i-make-flexbox-children-100-height-of-their-parent/16771324#16771324">David Storey's answer</a>, my workaround is:</p>
<pre><code>.flex-2 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Note that <code>height: 100%</code> <strong>must be removed</strong> from the child component (see comments).</p>
<p>Alternatively to <code>align-items</code>, you can use <code>align-self</code> just on the <code>.flex-2-child</code> item you want stretched.</p>

Q: How to exclude packages from CheckStyle analysis in a mavenized multi-module project? A: <p>This may bee a noobish question, but is there any more code in your checkstyle definition?</p>

<p>Usually we have something like this:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;fileset dir="src"&gt;
&lt;include name="**/*.java"/&gt;
&lt;exclude name="com/myproject/util/*.java"/&gt;
&lt;/fileset&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Where you need to say where to start scanning (source folder), what type of files to include (usually *.java) and what to exclude.
In my opinion you are trying to validate too much, and not necessary things. Checkstyle is used for validation developers code, not IDE config files.</p>
